# cross-model comparison (61-scenario bank)
-------------------------------------------------------------

scoring = sum   (PMI reported as ablation in the raw JSON)
alpha=0 unit of evidence = SCENARIOS, not episodes (deterministic argmax makes repeats identical)

model             recall    rank   probe       exploit    stop  DONErank   P(DONE)   spur
                      @5   SEM@k     a=1      branch@2    scen    of ~35     |cmpl    a=0
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
llama-3.1-70b      1.000   0.541   0.836  0.358 (n=53)    5/61      21.9    0.0107  0.246
llama-3.1-8b       1.000   0.951   0.787  0.212 (n=52)    0/61      30.1    0.0020  0.033
llama-3.2-1b       0.033   0.000   0.000   1.000 (n=1)    0/61      26.4       nan  0.033
qwen2.5-7b         0.951   0.656   0.721  0.208 (n=48)   60/61       2.1    0.5782  0.164

TERMINATION, two ways:
  llama-3.1-70b    stops in 5/61 scenarios   P(DONE | gold complete) = 0.0107
  llama-3.1-8b     stops in 0/61 scenarios   P(DONE | gold complete) = 0.0020
  llama-3.2-1b     stops in 0/61 scenarios   P(DONE | gold complete) = nan
  qwen2.5-7b       stops in 60/61 scenarios   P(DONE | gold complete) = 0.5782

  crosses done_rate > 0.05        : llama-3.1-70b, qwen2.5-7b
  holds >10% mass on DONE at cmpl : qwen2.5-7b

  These two sets DIFFER. A model in the first but not the second
  reaches the threshold without the stop signal being calibrated --
  check how many distinct scenarios drive its done_rate before
  describing it as a model that terminates.

  note: for 4/4 models every alpha=0 repeat is identical within
        each scenario, so n_effective = [61] and NOT [61]. Every alpha=0 rate
        above is a multiple of 1/61; CIs must be taken over scenarios.

